I sit in the government office.
An official calls my name.
I go to the desk.
He looks at my application.
He asks me.
"What is your phone number?"
I say my new number.
"Nine, eight, seven, six, five..."
"...four, three, two, one, zero," I say.
He writes that number.
Then he asks again.
"Do you have a local driving license?"
I reply.
"No, I do not have a driving license."
He nods his head.
He gives a paper to me.
I sign the paper.
My registration is complete.
